WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.220
Spider-Man: No Way Home is one of the MCU's
biggest successes, both in terms of critical

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.420
response and box office numbers.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.519
While the world is still reeling from the
movie's shock cameos, there were plenty of

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:17.390
monumental moments in the film that didn't
include you-know-who.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.500
Of course, Aunt May's death is easily No Way
Home's most devastating moment, but the ending

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.110
wasn't an easy pill to swallow, either.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:30.160
After Doctor Strange performs the spell that
makes the world forget Peter Parker, MJ and

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.710
Ned's memories are wiped, and Peter chooses
not to tell them about their past together.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.570
At the end of the movie, fans are left wondering
if MJ and Ned will ever remember who Peter

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.570
really is.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.600
Of course, many people will be holding out
hope that MJ and Ned are going to remember

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.290
Peter as they once did, and if that's the
case, it's bound to occur in a future Spider-Man

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.290
movie.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.900
But how could it actually happen?

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:57.860
Well, Sony producer Amy Pascal recently confirmed
to Fandango that the studios are getting ready

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.220
to make the next Spider-Man film.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:05.019
She also noted that Sony and Marvel are looking
at doing three more films, so Peter Parker

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:08.759
will have plenty of time to revert MJ and
Ned to their old selves.

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:13.359
Obviously, any ideas about how this will go
down are bound to be purely speculative in

00:01:13.359 --> 00:01:14.359
nature.

00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:18.159
Luckily, there are probably an infinite amount
of ways in which MJ and Ned might remember

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:21.759
Peter, especially now that the multiverse
has been fully unleashed.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:26.350
The simplest way, however, would be to have
Doctor Strange perform another spell.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.930
Naturally, Strange would need some convincing
since Stephen also doesn't remember Peter.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:34.479
But you could argue that it wouldn't be too
hard for Peter to convince him that they have

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:38.979
a history if the youngster just explains some
of the events that occurred on Titan during

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:40.509
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:45.079
Only the heroes who were there on Titan could
possibly know what happened, and Strange would

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:48.599
quickly accept the possibility his memory
has been tampered with.

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:50.240
"I'm Peter, by the way."

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.240
"Doctor Strange."

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.429
"Oh, we're using our made-up names.

00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:56.279
I'm Spider-Man, then."

00:01:56.279 --> 00:02:00.779
After all, No Way Home makes clear that he
has performed the spell before, so it's not

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:03.929
like the mind-erasing trick would seem unusual
to him.

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:08.349
As simple as this idea is, that's the problem
— it's a little too simple.

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:12.810
If Ned and MJ's memories are to be restored,
it'll likely be in a more dramatic fashion

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.439
than simply asking Strange to make things
right.

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:20.360
With so many projects in the works in the
MCU and dozens of characters spread throughout

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.670
them, it's not a far-fetched idea to think
someone else outside of the Spider-Man films

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.150
can help with Ned and MJ's amnesia.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:32.390
Wanda Maximoff is now more powerful than ever
as the Scarlet Witch, and we know she's dabbled

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.350
in mind control on occasion.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.430
Wanda is a trickier player than Strange, however,
and you wouldn't want her putting illusions

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.140
into Ned and MJ's heads.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.909
Still, maybe there's a more sensitive tweak
to her powers via which she can undo Strange's

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:45.909
spell.

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:49.120
In this case, though, there would have to
be some reason for Peter and Wanda to meet

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.120
up.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.280
While Elizabeth Olsen is set to appear in
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.930
it seems unlikely that Holland will make a
cameo — and who knows what the MCU has in

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.659
store for Wanda after that movie is released?

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:06.030
One character who is rumored to show up in
the second Doctor Strange flick is Charles

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.030
Xavier.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:11.599
Professor X knows a thing or two about mind
control, and if he effectively becomes canon

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:16.030
in the MCU, he might be someone whose powers
are available to Peter.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.700
With all the mind powers in his arsenal, it's
almost a guarantee that Professor X could

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.180
retrieve erased memories from a subject, especially
when they live on in someone else.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:30.349
That, of course, is assuming that Xavier even
makes it out of Multiverse of Madness.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:34.450
There are plenty of other characters who could
also help in the quest to revert the memories

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.430
of Peter's friends, some of whom we haven't
even met yet.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:41.920
Whoever it might be who lights the spark,
here's hoping it happens soon — because

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.980
what is the MCU Spider-Man without his Ned
and MJ?

